WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.367
Guys, I don't know if you
did see last Friday's show,

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.901
but Jimmy Kimmel hosted
"The Tonight Show,"

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:09.534
and I flew to L.A. and I hosted
"Jimmy Kimmel Live!"

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:11.334
And it was so fun. It was weird.

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:13.200
It was an April Fools' Day
prank.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.567
How did it feel?
What was it like?

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:17.834
-Uh, bad.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.000
Right?
-What do you mean it was bad?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.934
-Nobody -- We didn't have fun
here at all.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:24.767
-Oh. [ Laughs ]
Thank you so much.

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.467
Thank you for telling me that.
-It was a delight.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:27.701
-Tariq, did you have --

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.734
-It was awesome.
It was awesome, Jimmy.

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:31.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:36.100
To see you, you know, spreading
your love to the West Coast.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.534
It was -- I loved it.
-Spreading my love?

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:40.367
-Yeah, yeah, you know.
I loved it, man.

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.267
-You saw the West Coast,
what I did?

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.601
-Sure. We saw them chanting,
"Fallon, Fallon!"

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:45.734
It was crazy, man.

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.067
-Yeah.
Everyone started chanting.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:48.501
-You know,
you should have stayed, man.

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:51.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.734
-Wow!
-Why'd I come back?

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:56.767
...the way they treat me here.

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:58.501
It was so fun to see
because I know we have

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:01.400
the same job really,
but it's very different

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.801
the way we go about producing it
and all that stuff.

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.601
He has a great crew of people
over there.

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.167
And everyone
was really super nice

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:10.734
and wanted to make sure
Jimmy was taken care of here,

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:13.000
but they wanted to make sure
I was getting taken care of.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.601
So, I remember going to the
floor and seeing his desk.

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:18.000
Also you're really close
on his show.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.300
Like, the audience.
You're about how far away?

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.901
-A mile?
-Yeah, two miles.

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.734
His show, you're really close.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.133
It's a studio in a theater,

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.133
so you're like maybe 3 feet away
from the audience.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.968
-Oho.
-Yeah, it was interesting.

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:35.968
So, I was sitting there
and I was going to the desk,

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:39.934
and C.K. this guy who works
in props, he comes over.

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:43.267
He's like, "Mr. Fallon, we have
your spit cup here for you."

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:45.000
I go, "Alright. Thank you
very much. I appreciate it."

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.267
And then I'm going through it
and I go, "Spit cup?"

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:48.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:50.367
Is that, like, a thing?

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:52.334
I don't have a spit cup.
What does that mean?

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:53.501
-For chewing tobacco?

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:54.901
-I didn't know
what he was talking about.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.767
It was a cup
filled with tissues.

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:59.868
And I was like, "Is that a thing
that people think I do?

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:01.567
Do I spit?"

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:04.234
Do I have a saliva thing?
I don't know what that was.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.534
They go, "Here's your spit cup."

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:07.367
So, I go, "This is so weird."

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:10.100
And, so, I guess what happened
was I had told --

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.868
They go, "What do you want?"
I go, "I don't want anything.

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:13.968
You know, behind the desk,
there's really not much.

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:18.000
But I was like, "I like gum
every now and then."

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.133
Just to have fresh breath
when talking to my guests.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:24.501
And so I guess he made a cup
to put my gum in after I chew.

00:02:24.501 --> 00:02:26.534
I don't know.
I don't even do that either.

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:28.634
I usually put it in a tissue
or something like that.

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:31.267
But anyways --
But we made a short video

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:33.901
of behind the scenes of what
I witnessed when I was there.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:36.033
I just thought you may be
interested in seeing that,

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.267
how they do it.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:39.601
Here's me in L.A.
hosting "Jimmy Kimmel Live!"

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:43.033
-Jimmy Kimmel!

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:45.367
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:47.234
I'm confused.
Who's more confused?

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:49.267
Me or you guys? I have no idea.

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:50.968
Guillermo,
you know who I am, right?

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:53.000
-Yeah, yeah. Jimmy.
Yeah, Jimmy.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.801
[ Laughter ]
-That's correct.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.400
-...this intro here.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.300
-[ Laughs ]
Hey, good to see you.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.467
How you doing?
Nice to see you.

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.367
-This is just for you
to spit your gum in.

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.701
-Oh, perfect.
Thank you very much.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:04.133
To -- Say it again.

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.834
-It's for you
to spit your gum in.

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:08.300
-Spit into.
Yeah, okay, thank you.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.901
Is that something I do?
What have you heard?

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:15.267
I don't spit in things.
Spittoon was on my rider?

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:17.167
"Here's your cup to spit into"?

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:21.033
Welcome back
to "Jimmy Kimmel Live!"

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.067
I am Jimmy Fallon.
Let's just start the show.

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:25.968
You guys want to start the show?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:30.334
[ Fake-spits ]
Our first guest tonight --

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:33.367
We're already one spit into it.
Let's see how...

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:35.133
-There he is.

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:38.033
-Wow! Whoa. Wow.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.701
Wow. He's all -- Oh, please.
Oh, please. Really?

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:45.100
You see him enough.
Why would you clap for him?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.467
Oh, my God. Big deal.

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:49.968
-How's that [bleep] hole in L.A.
that you're working in?

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:53.634
You've been in L.A.
for, like, four hours,

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:58.267
and already you are very tan
and I am as white as a sheet.

00:03:58.267 --> 00:04:01.200
Everybody can hear Jimmy, right,
well here in the studio? Yeah?

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
Okay. Great. Okay. Good.

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.968
-That didn't quite sound as loud
as the crew over here.

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:10.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:13.734
Are you not entertained?!

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:18.300
[ Crew chanting "Fallon!" ]

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.901
-I'm fine staying here.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:22.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:26.167
-This is so fun.
This is so weird.

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:27.767
It's a comfy chair.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:31.701
It's much better than my chair.
My gosh.

00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:33.834
Really, I'm really writing down
all complaints.

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:35.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:38.167
I don't have a spit cup.
I don't have any of this stuff.

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.067
This changed my whole life.

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:42.734
This is fun. I love it.
Thanks for having me!

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:45.067
Yeah, that was a little
behind the scenes there.

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:48.868
It was interesting.

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:52.567
Jen, Sharon, Aaron, Irwin,
thank you, guys, so much.

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:54.167
They took care of me.

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:58.501
Mickey, Alec Potter.
Gary, Danny were the writers.

00:04:58.501 --> 00:04:59.868
Guillermo, of course.
Thank you.

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:02.334
Cleto and the Cletones.
And, of course, Jimmy and Molly.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.133
Thank you so much
for taking care of me

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:06.300
and having me
and pulling this off.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.801
It was a crazy idea.

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:11.567
Jimmy had this idea
maybe four years ago or longer,

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:13.300
maybe five years.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.767
We were out to dinner when
he did a show here in Brooklyn.

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:17.133
And he was like,
"Wouldn't it be fun

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.000
for April Fools'
if we switched places?"

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.367
And I was like, "Yeah."

00:05:20.367 --> 00:05:21.934
But I go, "It's a lot."

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:23.400
I mean, we got to fly to L.A.
He's got to fly --

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.133
It's a lot to pull off.
And we did it.

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:26.834
We pulled it off.

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:28.400
I want to thank
Justin Timberlake, too,

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:32.501
for pretending to be Matt Damon,
which was funny.

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:35.067
Also over here --
Oh, and, Chippy, of course.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:37.167
And here, Hugh Jackman,
Bridget Everett,

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:39.200
and, of course,
Red hot Chili Peppers.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:44.601
On my way out, I saw C.K.
as I was leaving.

00:05:44.601 --> 00:05:46.000
I go, "Take care, buddy."

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.434
And he goes,
"We got you a little present."

00:05:47.434 --> 00:05:48.667
I go, "Oh, thanks."

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:50.834
And he got me a brass spittoon.
-Aww.

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:53.300
-So I wanted to say thank you
very much. I appreciate that.

